--- tensor -- host-side dense n-d tensor functions (f64, row-major).
---
--- Single source of truth for the `tensor` host-function surface: 9 ops
--- covering construction (`zeros`, `ones`, `from_list`), projection
--- (`shape`, `to_list`), and algebra (`add`, `matmul`, `conv2d`,
--- `batch_norm`). A *runtime* (catopt
--- is the first consumer) composes this package by building a `HandlModule`
--- with the Rust `OpRegistry` this repo ships (`tensor_op_registry`), so
--- the `tensor.*` string callees resolve to native impls; nothing in the
--- eval engine or language data knows what a tensor is.
---
--- The tensor value is data on the `serde_json::Value` boundary —
--- `{"__tensor__": {"shape": [d, ...], "data": [x, ...], "dtype": "f64"}}`
--- — following the `{"__bytes__": ...}` tagged convention (ADR-0083 §2.1).
--- `shape` is the extent per axis, `data` the flat row-major payload whose
--- length is the product of `shape`, `dtype` the element type (only `f64`
--- for now). The tag keeps a tensor unambiguous next to user records while
--- staying a plain object to engines that have no `Tensor` scalar type —
--- promoting one in `value_types.yaml` later changes no wire shape.
---
--- All 9 functions are FFI atoms: a tensor has no literal syntax and no
--- eval-vocabulary constructor, so construction, projection, and algebra
--- cannot be expressed as pure handl arrows. The `op`/`handle` declaration
--- form (ADR-0077 Phase 2) declares the interface; the Rust `Function`
--- impls in `src/ops.rs` provide the logic and are registered in an
--- `OpRegistry` that dispatches each `op` to its native impl.
---
--- `tensor.from_list(xs)` infers the shape from nested number arrays and
--- rejects ragged input; `tensor.add(a, b)` requires identical shapes
--- (broadcasting is follow-up); `tensor.matmul(a, b)` is rank-2 × rank-2
--- `(m×k)·(k×n)` for now (batched matmul is follow-up).
---
--- `conv2d` / `batch_norm` take *positional optional* trailing
--- parameters: a `null` (or a missing argument) selects the default, so
--- `conv2d(x, w, null, [2, 2])` is "no bias, stride 2×2, no padding" and
--- `batch_norm(x, g, b, m, v)` uses the default `eps = 1e-5`. Both are
--- NCHW: `conv2d` consumes `input [N, C_in, H, W]` × `weight
--- [C_out, C_in/groups, kH, kW]` (naive cross-correlation — no kernel
--- flip — with `bias?` rank-1 `[C_out]`, `stride?`/`padding?` an int or
--- `[h, w]` pair, `groups?` a positive int); `batch_norm` is the
--- eval-mode `(x − μ)/√(σ²+ε)·γ+β` per channel with rank-1 `[C]`
--- `gamma`/`beta`/`mean`/`var` parameters.
---
--- ## Capability declarations (ADR-0077 Phase 4)
--- tensor.zeros -- a tensor of `shape` filled with 0.0.
--- tensor.ones -- a tensor of `shape` filled with 1.0.
--- tensor.from_list -- a tensor whose flat row-major data is `xs`' nested number arrays (ragged rejected).
--- tensor.to_list -- the nested number arrays for tensor `t` (inverse of from_list).
--- tensor.shape -- the extent-per-axis list of tensor `t`.
--- tensor.add -- elementwise `a + b` (identical shapes required).
--- tensor.matmul -- `(m×k)·(k×n)` dense matrix product of two rank-2 tensors.
--- tensor.conv2d -- NCHW conv2d `(input, weight, bias?, stride?, padding?, groups?)`.
--- tensor.batch_norm -- eval-mode batch norm `(input, gamma, beta, mean, var, eps?)`.
cap "tensor.zeros"
cap "tensor.ones"
cap "tensor.from_list"
cap "tensor.to_list"
cap "tensor.shape"
cap "tensor.add"
cap "tensor.matmul"
cap "tensor.conv2d"
cap "tensor.batch_norm"
op "tensor.zeros" : (List Int) -> Tensor
  guarantee: True
op "tensor.ones" : (List Int) -> Tensor
  guarantee: True
op "tensor.from_list" : Array -> Tensor
  guarantee: True
op "tensor.to_list" : Tensor -> Array
  guarantee: True
op "tensor.shape" : Tensor -> (List Int)
  guarantee: True
op "tensor.add" : (Tensor * Tensor) -> Tensor
  guarantee: True
op "tensor.matmul" : (Tensor * Tensor) -> Tensor
  guarantee: True
--- conv2d(input, weight, bias?, stride?, padding?, groups?) — variadic;
--- `null` at an optional position selects the default (see the header).
op "tensor.conv2d" : Value... -> Tensor
  guarantee: True
--- batch_norm(input, gamma, beta, mean, var, eps?) — variadic; `null`
--- `eps` selects the 1e-5 default.
op "tensor.batch_norm" : Value... -> Tensor
  guarantee: True
handle "tensor.zeros" with rust_tensor_zeros
handle "tensor.ones" with rust_tensor_ones
handle "tensor.from_list" with rust_tensor_from_list
handle "tensor.to_list" with rust_tensor_to_list
handle "tensor.shape" with rust_tensor_shape
handle "tensor.add" with rust_tensor_add
handle "tensor.matmul" with rust_tensor_matmul
handle "tensor.conv2d" with rust_tensor_conv2d
handle "tensor.batch_norm" with rust_tensor_batch_norm

--- The `tensor` namespace record — `from "host-tensor" import tensor` binds
--- the whole surface at once (each field is the qualified-name string the
--- `op` declarations export, so `tensor.matmul(a, b)` dispatches through
--- `call_host` exactly like the per-name imports do).
export tensor := {
  zeros: "tensor.zeros",
  ones: "tensor.ones",
  from_list: "tensor.from_list",
  to_list: "tensor.to_list",
  shape: "tensor.shape",
  add: "tensor.add",
  matmul: "tensor.matmul",
  conv2d: "tensor.conv2d",
  batch_norm: "tensor.batch_norm"
}
